    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.Performance">PERFORMANCE</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.OptimizeGames">Optimize games at launch</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.OptimizeGamesTip">Enables all launch optimisation. Applies the selected CPU mode, priority, power saving and launcher background. It does not change Windows settings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.CpuMode">CPU mode</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.CpuModeSummary">Lets you forcibly override how load is distributed across CPU cores.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.CpuModeAutoOnly">Only automatic mode is available for this CPU.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.CpuAuto">Auto</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.CpuAutoTip">Windows chooses the cores for the game and takes P-cores and E-cores into account. This is the safe default for most games and forces nothing.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.CpuPerformance">P-cores</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.CpuPerformanceTip">The game runs only on performance cores (P-cores). Can improve stability and 1% lows in CPU-bound games and emulators. May lower FPS in heavily threaded games.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.CpuEfficiency">E-cores</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.CpuEfficiencyTip">The game runs only on efficiency cores (E-cores). Usually gives lower FPS than P-cores or Auto. Use it for background tasks or testing.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.CpuL3">1 CCD</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.CpuL3Tip">Keeps the game on one CCD or L3 domain. Helps dual-CCD AMD Ryzen avoid cross-chiplet jumps. No effect on single-CCD Ryzen.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.Priority">Priority</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.PrioritySummary">Lets you forcibly override the game process priority.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.PriorityNormal">Auto</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.PriorityNormalTip">Auto. Standard Windows priority. The game competes with background tasks as usual. Suitable when nothing heavy runs in the background.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.PriorityAbove">Medium</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.PriorityAboveTip">Medium. Slightly above normal. The game gets more CPU time under background load while the system stays responsive. A safe choice for most games.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.PriorityHigh">High</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.PriorityHighTip">High priority. The game pushes background tasks aside and can help during recording, browsing or antivirus scans. May reduce system responsiveness, use it when needed.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.Timer">Timer</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.TimerSummary">Raises the system timer precision. Usually not required.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.TimerOff">Off</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.TimerOffTip">Standard Windows timer. Recommended.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.Timer1">1 ms</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.Timer1Tip">Raises precision to 1 ms. Can improve frame pacing and slightly increases power usage.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.TimerHalf">0.5 ms</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.TimerHalfTip">Maximum precision. Use it only when frame pacing problems occur.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.DisableEcoQos">Disable game power saving</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.DisableEcoQosSummary">Remove EcoQoS and power throttling from the game process.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.DisableEcoQosTip">Windows can slow processes down through EcoQoS. This option removes that limit from the game. It slightly increases power usage.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.LauncherBackground">Launcher in background</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.LauncherBackgroundSummary">Lower the launcher priority while a game is running.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Loc.Settings.LauncherBackgroundTip">While a game is running, the launcher stays in the background at low priority and does not compete for CPU. Its priority is restored after the game exits.</sys:String>
